{"ts": 0.0986, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mPATH is a list\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[92mPATH\u001b[0m holds folders separated by colons. When you type a command name,\r\nthe shell looks in those folders, in order, and runs the first match.\r\n", "len": 180}
{"ts": 0.098616, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n  \u001b[92mecho \"$PATH\"\u001b[0m                  \u001b[90m# one long line\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mecho \"$PATH\" | tr : '\\n'\u001b[0m      \u001b[90m# one folder per line\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mcommand -v ls\u001b[0m                 \u001b[90m# the full name of ls: its folder, then ls\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nA program in a folder that is not on the list is not found by name.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m> Run all three, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 364}
{"ts": 0.101534, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
